  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A tube of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is filled completely with an incompressible liquid of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> and closed at both ends. The tube is then rotated in horizontal plane about one of its ends with a uniform angular velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mi>F</mi></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;be the force exerted by the liquid at the other end then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> will be _____ .",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Considering an element of tube of length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>d</mo><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;having mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>d</mo><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;at a distance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;from right end as shown in figure below.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6a45f03d-0632-4ae7-82b8-0827319b4916-image.png\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 95px;\" /></p><p>Now, force acting of that element is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>Integrating the above relation for whole length of tube, we have&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo>d</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>L</mi></mfrac><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfrac><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>L</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><msqrt><mi>F</mi></msqrt></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><msqrt><mi>F</mi></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>16</mn></msqrt><msqrt><mi>F</mi></msqrt></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Hence, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>",
